# Desecration Demon: "any opponent may sacrifice a creature of their choice" - one creature, not more (CR 701.21a). At its beginning of combat on turn 2 Bot2, holding a Memnite and an
# Ornithopter, is refused when it chooses both and sacrifices the Memnite alone: the Ornithopter stays, and the Demon is tapped with one +1/+1 counter, a 7/7.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Desecration Demon
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Desecration Demon.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
! Bot2.Choose(Memnite; Ornithopter)
Bot2.Choose(Memnite)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Memnite
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Desecration Demon.Power = 7
Bot1.Battlefield.Desecration Demon.Tapped = true
